  WHAT IS INCLUDED

  29 Kotlin source files, redistributed under the package `com.mihon`:

    core/mihon/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/mihon/**   (27 files)
    core/mihon/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/mihon/**  (2 files)

  They provide the Compose settings framework — preference widgets, the preference
  screen scaffold, settings search — and the Material components it needs. Mihon
  does not publish these as a library, which is why they are vendored.

  Every one of the 29 has an identified upstream counterpart. The per-file mapping
  is in core/mihon/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/mihon/readme.md.

  THESE FILES HAVE BEEN MODIFIED

  All 29 differ from upstream. The extent varies, and this notice is precise about
  that rather than claiming more than is true:

    * Most are ported rather than copied. The package was changed from
      `eu.kanade.*` / `tachiyomi.*` to `com.mihon.*`, and Android-only and
      Mihon-specific APIs were replaced so the code builds for Kotlin
      Multiplatform. In material/SettingsItems.kt, for example, `ImageVector` and
      Mihon's icon set become Compose `Painter` and `painterResource`, Moko
      `StringResource` becomes Compose Resources `StringResource`, and
      `Preference<T>` becomes `PreferenceData<T>`: 30 upstream lines removed and 46
      added, ours 474 lines against upstream's 458.
      material/AppBar.kt is the largest divergence: 100 upstream lines removed and
      57 added, ours 405 against upstream's 449.

    * Three files — material/Constants.kt, material/Pill.kt and
      material/Typography.kt — differ from upstream in the `package` line and in
      nothing else. They are otherwise verbatim copies.

    * Three are not same-name copies. common/preference/PreferenceData.kt is
      upstream's Preference.kt renamed; presentation/Navigation.kt keeps one
      declaration lifted out of upstream's Navigator.kt; presentation/settings/
      Search.kt is a substantial rework of upstream's SettingsSearchScreen.kt.

  No individual file carries a change notice. This notice covers all of them,
  which is how this project satisfies section 4(b) of the Apache License: the
  modification is stated prominently and in one place, rather than by editing 29
  headers that would then drift out of date.

  BASELINE

  The tree entered this repository on 2026-09-08 in commit 92b3ea92 ("Compose
  work (#3151)"), with further changes in 6b7a81ab and 99ce06dd on 2026-09-12. It
  was vendored upstream in recloudstream/cloudstream and inherited here.

  The upstream Mihon commit it was taken from was not recorded at the time and
  cannot be recovered from this repository. The file-by-file comparison summarised
  above was made against Mihon's `main` branch as fetched on 2026-10-07; `main`
  moves, so those line counts are a snapshot, not a fixed fact. A reviewer wanting
  to re-diff should start from Mihon's history on or before 2026-09-08.

